            <ArticleTitle>Strut fracture: a further concern with drug-eluting stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>949-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e3282f03bad</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A potential cause of drug-eluting stent restenosis is strut fracture. To date, few cases have been reported in the available literature and a best treatment method has not been established. We describe two cases of sirolimus-eluting stent fracture combined with focal restenosis and also review those previously reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
